    "poster_id": 195510,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b21b36bfc3bad4b81f5aed2c6f5613bc98403ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" > is a natural number. Find the maximum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > such that there are real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436dec2c978e019eab22cf2ea0c1b0335798d92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,...,a_n \\in [0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" > (not necessarily distinct) that for every natural number like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577b861c7d1cdab4dc26f0485f3966ca44eb745b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" > , sum of some <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" >-</span>s is <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"8\" height=\"16\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Navid Safaei </i>",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose that $n\\ge3$ is a natural number. Find the maximum value $k$ such that there are real numbers $a_1,a_2,...,a_n \\in [0,1)$ (not necessarily distinct) that for every natural number like $j \\le k$ , sum of some $a_i$-s is $j$.\n\n[i]Proposed by Navid Safaei [/i]",
