    "topic_id": 3032970,
    "poster_id": 195510,
    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > is cyclic quadrilateral and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > is the center of its circumcircle. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91fdb194e20bb384f58aa43713a73f03084ed52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\cap BC = E$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f65bca21157e408cb958375907a23d9a8d8f2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\cap BD = F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" >.</span> Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > is tanget to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\"  width=\"29\" height=\"12\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" > is a diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is orthocenter of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7500a1e02eb832d871945dd5cbaadef0f48b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EPQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" >.</span> Prove that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9d3474e139c8e1c2f5902c3cb42d7e47fa7e0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > is passing through center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" ><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Mahdi Etesami Fard </i>",
    "post_canonical": "$ABCD$ is cyclic quadrilateral and $O$ is the center of its circumcircle. Suppose that $AD \\cap BC = E$ and $AC \\cap BD = F$. Circle $\\omega$ is tanget to line $AC$ and $BD$. $PQ$ is a diameter of $\\omega$ that $F$ is orthocenter of $EPQ$. Prove that line $OE$ is passing through center of $\\omega$\n\n[i]Proposed by Mahdi Etesami Fard [/i]",
