    "poster_id": 195510,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345499c056313b266d6f26e93859f62eb1fda2b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} &lt; s &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" > . An insect flying on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e861e10e1c19918756b9c8b7717684593c63aeb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" > . If it is on point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" > , it jump into point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06699bd6482319759881ba43ac0238b5188f7df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ a\\times s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" > or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fb015e32b3dab190e419ee3d3197015cc55452.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1) \\times s +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" >  . For every real number <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0ef9494fa8a1eac19f0e1ba3bc691da3de480e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le c \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" >,</span> Prove that insect can jump that after some jumps , it has a distance less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c4a9a25bb64ae1eaa5aafc7baff0efc1006803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{1402}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" > from point <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"8\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Navid Safaei </i>",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose $\\frac{1}{2} < s < 1$ . An insect flying on $[0,1]$ . If it is on point $a$ , it jump into point $ a\\times s$ or $(a-1) \\times s +1$  . For every real number $0 \\le c \\le 1$, Prove that insect can jump that after some jumps , it has a distance less than $\\frac {1}{1402}$ from point $c$.\n\n[i]Proposed by Navid Safaei [/i]",
