    "topic_id": 3033477,
    "poster_id": 195510,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" > non-empty subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/2869a0fdb8652d1df9de882cb42f4085513a15d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ \\big\\{0,1,2,...,2n-1\\big\\} $\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"149\" height=\"24\" > that sum of the number of elements of these subsets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d4468d74243bcd2024fa40b5d18ea7806656cbeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ \\binom{2n+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"81\" height=\"55\" > . Prove that we can choose one element from every subset that some of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/0989e1bd02750c086bc30fa0fd65c9e68ab0fa49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ \\binom{2n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"50\" height=\"55\" ><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Morteza Saghafian and Afrouz Jabalameli </i>",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose that we have $2n$ non-empty subset of $ \\big\\{0,1,2,...,2n-1\\big\\} $ that sum of the number of elements of these subsets is $ \\binom{2n+1}{2}$ . Prove that we can choose one element from every subset that some of them is $ \\binom{2n}{2}$\n\n[i]Proposed by Morteza Saghafian and Afrouz Jabalameli [/i]",
